<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>dev.ikigai-rs.cms</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/brian/.cargo/bin/cms-server</string>
  </array>
  <!-- The semantic-CMS reading room. All configuration lives in
       ~/.config/ikigai/cms.toml (page_port 8090 = the URL you open, wire_port 4434 =
       the internal WebTransport face); flags would override it, but there are none
       here on purpose: config home, not flags, not env vars.

       This file is versioned in ikigai-cms-web at deploy/macos/; the copy launchd
       loads lives in ~/Library/LaunchAgents/. Copying it there changes nothing until
       the next bootstrap.

       Points at ~/.cargo/bin rather than the repo's target/release build: a target/
       binary dies on `cargo clean` and gets silently swapped by the next debug build,
       so launchd would serve whatever last landed there.

       PREREQUISITE: the install command under "Install as a service" in the repo's
       README. It builds the server feature against the committed lock and replaces
       the installed binary. It is not spelled out here because its flags begin with
       two hyphens, and two hyphens in a row are illegal inside an XML comment:
       plutil tolerates them, but Python's plistlib and every standard XML parser
       reject the whole file. Every binary in this crate sits behind a required
       feature, so an install WITHOUT the server feature compiles everything, warns
       that no binaries are available, and exits 0 having installed nothing.

       TWO GRANT HAZARDS on first bootstrap (see the LWCR/TCC notes): it reads the
       source jail under ~/Dropbox/org-mode-files, and the passkey store is the macOS
       Keychain; both can be denied silently to a launchd-spawned process. Bootstrap
       it with someone at the screen, then check /tmp/ikigai-cms.log for a clean start
       rather than assuming. Bootout, wait, then bootstrap after any edit; never
       kickstart. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key><true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key><integer>5</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/tmp/ikigai-cms.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/tmp/ikigai-cms.log</string>
</dict></plist>
